  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A conducting square loop of side $\\mathrm{L}$ and resistance $\\mathrm{R}$ moves in its plane with a uniform velocity v perpendicular to one of its side. A magnetic induction $\\mathrm{B}$ constant in time and space, pointing perpendicular and into the plane of the loop exists everywhere.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/v3-1Mt3mK4D2OS5PERmiMAk_YvGxnqyAuKIeBkon8vw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nThe current induced in the loop is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GMG6K",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{B} \\ell \\mathrm{v}}{\\mathrm{R}}$ clockwise",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pwN2Z",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{B} \\ell \\mathrm{v}}{\\mathrm{R}}$ anticlockwise",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oZODu",
      "text": "$\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~B} \\ell v}{\\mathrm{R}}$ anticlockwise",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bYdaO",
      "text": "zero",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since the magnetic field is uniform the flux $f$ through the square loop at any time $t$ is constant, because\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{f}=\\mathrm{B} \\times \\mathrm{A}=\\mathrm{B} \\times \\mathrm{L}^{2}=\\text { constant } \\\\\r\n\r\n\\therefore \\varepsilon=-\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\phi}{\\mathrm{dt}}=\\text { zero }\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
